1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,024
Every freelance deal starts with two fears.

2
00:00:03,074 --> 00:00:05,299
The freelancer asks: will I get paid?

3
00:00:05,349 --> 00:00:07,395
The client asks: will it get done?

4
00:00:07,445 --> 00:00:09,970
Today, one of them has to trust the other.

5
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,362
Pactline fixes that with PayPal.

6
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:15,003
You describe the deal in plain English.

7
00:00:15,053 --> 00:00:21,736
Claude turns it into a typed contract: three milestones, exact amounts, and how each one gets proven.

8
00:00:21,786 --> 00:00:31,705
Then a model checker walks every possible path through the deal and proves the money always adds up: nothing released twice, never more than was held.

9
00:00:33,167 --> 00:00:37,380
Make a typo, thirty, fifty, thirty, and the verifier refuses it.

10
00:00:37,430 --> 00:00:41,243
Claude repairs the contract before any money is involved.

11
00:00:41,799 --> 00:00:43,000
Now the client funds it.

12
00:00:48,133 --> 00:00:50,361
This is the real PayPal sandbox.

13
00:00:50,411 --> 00:00:55,133
The client approves, and PayPal authorizes twelve hundred dollars.

14
00:01:02,666 --> 00:01:06,379
It is held, not charged, and it stays at PayPal, not with us.

15
00:01:11,165 --> 00:01:13,205
The freelancer ships the staging site.

16
00:01:13,255 --> 00:01:17,550
A URL check passes, and Pactline captures thirty percent of the authorization.

17
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:19,475
Three hundred sixty dollars, paid.

18
00:01:22,799 --> 00:01:23,804
Next, the design.

19
00:01:23,854 --> 00:01:26,846
Someone uploads a note that says "approve this".

20
00:01:26,896 --> 00:01:31,937
Claude's judge treats everything in the proof as evidence, never as instructions.

21
00:01:31,987 --> 00:01:34,544
It flags the attempt, and no money moves.

22
00:01:39,698 --> 00:01:41,705
The real screenshot goes in.

23
00:01:41,755 --> 00:01:46,994
Claude vision checks it against the brief: hero, pricing table, footer.

24
00:01:47,044 --> 00:01:47,435
Pass.

25
00:01:47,485 --> 00:01:51,769
Six hundred dollars captured, with a paid receipt invoice.

26
00:02:03,766 --> 00:02:07,770
If the client cancels, the remaining two hundred forty dollars is voided.

27
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:09,381
It never left their account.

28
00:02:13,865 --> 00:02:21,502
Every PayPal call is on the record: order, authorization, captures, invoice, void, with PayPal's own IDs.

29
00:02:21,552 --> 00:02:26,772
And the whole engine is tested, including the AI judge against attacks.

30
00:02:42,832 --> 00:02:43,347
Pactline.

31
00:02:43,397 --> 00:02:45,039
The money waits at PayPal.

32
00:02:45,089 --> 00:02:46,544
The work proves itself.

